      "stories": [
        {
          "id": "mve7ubk6-4e83fu",
          "intentId": "mve7ubj2-f3ne9z",
          "title": "After the Wanting",
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "fragmentId": "op9",
              "text": "No scramble, no dread, no list running before your feet touch the floor. Just morning, and you, and the life that answered."
            },
            {
              "fragmentId": "ar-ab6",
              "text": "You tip well. You book the trip. You breathe. Enough stopped being a ceiling and became a floor: A home by the sea."
            },
            {
              "fragmentId": "se10",
              "text": "Your own handwriting in the margin of today's list looks different lately. Rounder. Unclenched."
            },
            {
              "fragmentId": "li-ab3",
              "text": "An opportunity lands in your inbox — the paid kind, the aligned kind. They find you regularly now, like the address finally got listed."
            },
            {
              "fragmentId": "wi7",
              "text": "Someone younger watches how you move through the day and quietly adjusts their own sails. You remember being them. You'd have loved proof like you."
            },
            {
              "fragmentId": "gr1",
              "text": "Gratitude arrives on its own now, uninvited, mid-afternoon — for the ordinary furniture of a life you once begged the sky for."
            },
            {
              "fragmentId": "cl6",
              "text": "Sleep takes you gently, the way it takes people with nothing to flee. Tomorrow will rhyme with today. That's the whole plan now."
            }
          ],
          "createdAt": "2026-10-18T19:26:00.966Z"
        },
        {
          "id": "mve7u3o9-dxcgnl",
          "intentId": "mve7tc04-8kywog",
          "title": "After the Wanting",
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "fragmentId": "op7",
              "text": "The day doesn't ask anything of you yet. It just waits, warm and unhurried, while you remember who you've become."
            },
            {
              "fragmentId": "ar-ca2",
              "text": "The first task of the day is one you'd do for free — and they pay you well for it. Strange and wonderful, how the intention held: my own design studio, with clients who trust my eye."
            },
            {
              "fragmentId": "se3",
              "text": "The air outside smells faintly of rain that already fell. Everything is rinsed, including — somehow — you."
            },
            {
              "fragmentId": "li-ca3",
              "text": "You decline a shiny thing that isn't yours to do, and the calendar breathes. Mastery is mostly subtraction, you've learned."
            },
            {
              "fragmentId": "wi7",
              "text": "Someone younger watches how you move through the day and quietly adjusts their own sails. You remember being them. You'd have loved proof like you."
            },
            {
              "fragmentId": "gr6",
              "text": "Somewhere in the day you feel it land — that this was once the dream. This exact, ordinary, extraordinary Tuesday. You feel proud, all the way through."
            },
            {
              "fragmentId": "cl2",
              "text": "You set tomorrow's one intention like a cup by the kettle, then let the day go completely. Sleep comes down like warm weather."
            },
            {
              "fragmentId": "proof-2",
              "text": "There is proof behind this memory now: Sent my portfolio to two studios I admire.. It is small enough to be real, and real enough to change what comes next."
            }
          ],
          "createdAt": "2026-10-18T19:25:50.746Z"
        }
      ],
      "actions": [
